        "id": "whitemane",
        "name": "Whitemane"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Yrel can help Tanks with a weak engage to force a fight by finding a good flank and can support the ones who lack peeling to protect the backline from aggressive enemy Heroes.\n\nThe Armor from Aegis of Light at Level 4 is great for protecting allied Heroes who lack mobility. Garrosh benefits from it more than other Heroes because it stacks with Armor Up.\n\nThe healing from Gift of the Naaru at Level 4 can be useful for playing in the offlane as a 2-man with Zarya on Braxis Holdout. This strategy allows you to have good damage and survivability on both lanes.\n\nThe ability to provide Movement Speed and remove some crowd control effects with Hand of Freedom at Level 4, together with the possibility to use Righteous Hammer defensively when needed, is quite useful for helping allied Heroes who are in trouble."
  },
  "counters": {
    "heroes": [
      {
        "id": "muradin",
        "name": "Muradin"
      },
      {
        "id": "malthael",
        "name": "Malthael"
      },
      {
        "id": "sgt-hammer",
        "name": "Sgt. Hammer"
      },
      {
        "id": "tracer",
        "name": "Tracer"
      },
      {
        "id": "stukov",
        "name": "Stukov"
      }
    ],
    "explanation": "Yrel suffers against Heroes that possess reliable crowd control effects who can interrupt her Basic Abilities as they are being channeled (Stuns and Silences) or who can interrupt Avenging Wrath during its jump animation (Roots and Knockbacks).\n\nShe also struggles against Heroes who can kite her from the distance or have a lot of mobility to deal damage without being hit in return. While laning, these Heroes could threaten a gank, forcing Yrel to use her Heroic Ability to stay alive.\n\nLast but not the least, Yrel is relatively weak to healing reduction effects (especially if having Ardent Defender as Heroic Ability), Armor reduction effects (especially if having Sacred Ground as Heroic Ability), and percent-based damage because they all reduce her survivability during team fights."
  },
